{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5570: \"[stitch] Implement cmd/users error handling and differential tests (srd096 R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\". This is an automated code generation task on branch `task/generation-run44-5570`. The task requires:\n   - Modifying `cmd/users/main.go` to add error handling, help output, and version output (though these already exist in the current code)\n   - Creating `cmd/users/users_test.go` with differential tests against the `gusers` GNU reference binary\n   - Ensuring exit code 0 on success (R2.1), exit code 1 on error (R2.2), and SIGPIPE handling (R2.3)\n   - All acceptance criteria must pass: tests pass with gusers, differential comparison of stdout/stderr/exit code, graceful skip without gusers, go vet clean, error handling matches GNU behavior\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: Run Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, compare stdout, stderr, exit code\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` / `testutils.BuildBinary` / `testutils.DiffTest` API for test harness\n   - CGo integration for reading utmpx database (`#include <utmpx.h>`)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - GNU coreutils reference binary naming: `gusers` (Homebrew g-prefix)\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for deterministic test output\n   - `exec.LookPath` with `t.Skip` for graceful degradation when reference binary absent\n   - Go build constraint: `go build -o bin/<name> ./cmd/<name>/`\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd096-users.yaml** (read)\n     - SRD for the `users` command\n     - R1 group: User listing (R1.1 read utmpx, R1.2 FILE argument, R1.3 no deduplication)\n     - R2 group: Exit codes and SIGPIPE (R2.1 exit 0 success, R2.2 exit 1 error, R2.3 SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no idle time, terminal, or remote host info\n     - Package imports: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys`\n\n   - **cmd/users/main.go** (read, to be modified)\n     - Already has complete implementation including: SIGPIPE handler, help/version flags, error handling for extra operands, unrecognized options, invalid options, utmpx reading via CGo\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Implements srd096-users R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1, R2.2, R2.3.\n     package main\n     \n     /*\n     #include <utmpx.h>\n     #include <stdlib.h>\n     */\n     import \"C\"\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"sort\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"unsafe\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: users [OPTION]... [FILE]\n     Output who is currently logged in according to FILE.\n     If FILE is not specified, use /var/run/utmpx.  /var/log/wtmpx as FILE is common.\n     \n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     \n     const versionText = `users (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         args := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         if len(args) > 1 {\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"users: extra operand '%s'\\n\", args[1])\n             fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'users --help' for more information.\")\n             os.Exit(1)\n         }\n         if len(args) == 1 {\n             cpath := C.CString(args[0])\n             C.utmpxname(cpath)\n             C.free(unsafe.Pointer(cpath))\n         }\n         names := readUsers()\n         if len(names) > 0 {\n             sort.Strings(names)\n             if _, err := fmt.Fprintln(os.Stdout, strings.Join(names, \" \")); err != nil {\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     \n     func readUsers() []string {\n         C.setutxent()\n         defer C.endutxent()\n         var names []string\n         for {\n             entry := C.getutxent()\n             if entry == nil { break }\n             if entry.ut_type != C.USER_PROCESS { continue }\n             name := C.GoString(&entry.ut_user[0])\n             names = append(names, name)\n         }\n         return names\n     }\n     \n     func parseArgs(args []string) []string {\n         var remaining []string\n         endOfFlags := false\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if endOfFlags {\n                 remaining = append(remaining, arg)\n                 continue\n             }\n             switch {\n             case arg == \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n                 os.Exit(0)\n             case arg == \"--\":\n                 endOfFlags = true\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--\"):\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"users: unrecognized option '%s'\\n\", arg)\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'users --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             case strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1:\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"users: invalid option -- '%c'\\n\", arg[1])\n                 fmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'users --help' for more information.\")\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             default:\n                 remaining = append(remaining, arg)\n             }\n         }\n         return remaining\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/users/users_test.go** (to be created)\n     - Needs differential tests following the project's shared protocol pattern\n     - Must use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gusers\")`\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - Key API: `DiffTest` struct, `RunDiffTests` function, `BuildBinary` function (in build.go)\n     - DiffTest fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the existing `cmd/users/main.go` already implements all R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 requirements (exit codes and SIGPIPE). The main.go may need minor modifications or may be sufficient as-is.\n   - The primary deliverable is creating `cmd/users/users_test.go` with differential tests covering: normal output, error cases (extra operands, unrecognized options, invalid options).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The massive task prompt containing the full task specification, project context, SRDs, source code, constitutions, constraints, requirements, design decisions, and acceptance criteria for task #5570.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Review whether `cmd/users/main.go` needs any modifications (the R2 requirements appear already implemented)\n   - Create `cmd/users/users_test.go` with differential tests against `gusers` covering:\n     - Normal invocation (no args) - prints logged-in users\n     - Error case: extra operand\n     - Error case: unrecognized option (e.g., `--foo`)\n     - Error case: invalid short option (e.g., `-x`)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/users/` to verify no errors\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/users/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just completed reading the two required files (srd096-users.yaml and cmd/users/main.go) and was about to begin implementation. The existing main.go already has all the R2 group functionality implemented (error handling, help/version output, SIGPIPE handling). The main deliverable is creating the test file `cmd/users/users_test.go` with differential tests. I need to:\n   1. Possibly review main.go for any gaps (it looks complete for R2.1-R2.3)\n   2. Write `cmd/users/users_test.go` following the differential testing pattern\n   3. Build and test\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/users/users_test.go` with differential tests. The test file should follow the shared protocol pattern from the task prompt:\n   ```\n   func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n       goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n       refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gusers\")\n       if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n       tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n       testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n   }\n   ```\n   Test cases should cover: no-args invocation, extra operand error (exit 1), unrecognized option error (exit 1), and invalid short option error (exit 1). Then verify with `go vet` and `go test`.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5570/e7ed4a09-fdb8-4b2b-9e65-1ed9f398610e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e7ed4a09-fdb8-4b2b-9e65-1ed9f398610e","uuid":"1c70129d-3418-43da-9c54-ac47cfc267a8","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:30:55.632Z","isSynthetic":true}
